# What must never reach the Docker build context.
#
# Without this file the context is ~28 GB (an 18 GB scratch directory, a 9 GB host virtualenv, node_modules,
# demo videos, model weights), the build spends minutes just uploading it, and `COPY . .` bakes all of it
# into the image. The .env exclusion is the important one: it holds the generated secrets, and an image
# carrying them would leak every credential to anyone who pulls it.

# Secrets and local configuration. Never in an image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.admin-token
*.pem
*.key

# Host virtualenv. The image builds its own with the right interpreter and platform wheels; copying the
# host one in would shadow it with binaries compiled for a different base.
.venv/
venv/

# Runtime scratch: exports, training runs, downloaded weights, intermediate artifacts. Regenerated on demand
# and by far the largest directory in the tree. .perception_work holds cloud-perception sweep intermediates
# and is nearly a gigabyte on a box that has run one.
.scratch/
scratch/
.perception_work/

# Web build inputs and outputs. web/Dockerfile runs `npm ci` and `next build` itself, so copying these in
# would both bloat the context and risk a node_modules built for the host's platform.
web/node_modules/
web/.next/
web/out/
node_modules/

# Model weights. Ultralytics fetches what it needs on first use, and the compose file mounts a named volume
# at /app/models so they persist across rebuilds instead of being baked into every image layer.
*.pt
*.onnx
*.engine
models/
# Ultralytics writes training runs here (weights, plots, results.csv). Output, not input.
runs/

# Version control and CI.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore

# Media and documentation that no runtime path reads.
demos/
docs/screenshots/
*.mp4
*.gif

# Python and tooling caches.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.import_linter_cache/
*.egg-info/
htmlcov/
.coverage

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.swp
